# Territory Painting

Status: DONE
Milestone: M1 Technical proofs
Dependencies: `02_DOMAIN_RULES.todo`, `03_PLAYER_CAMERA_INPUT.todo`

## Purpose

Prove deterministic, performant floor territory whose logical ownership matches its visual representation.

## Tasks

- [x] Implement paintable-surface registration.
- [x] Implement world-to-territory coordinate mapping.
- [x] Implement logical field storage.
- [x] Implement spray stamp commands.
- [x] Implement reset.
- [x] Implement coverage queries.
- [x] Implement territory sampling beneath a player.
- [x] Implement visual mask stamping.
- [x] Implement ownership debug overlay.
- [x] Implement sustained-spray benchmark.
- [x] Compare candidate CPU/GPU split approaches.
- [x] Record territory authority decision.
- [x] Add deterministic sequence tests.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Visual and logical ownership align for all test stamps.
- [x] Score is deterministic.
- [x] Full reset leaves no stale logical or visual paint.
- [x] Sustained spray meets provisional CPU/GPU budgets.
- [x] Memory usage is bounded and documented.
- [x] Territory can be sampled without GPU readback.

## Completion evidence

- Selected sandbox: `EntropyTag/Assets/EntropyTag/Scenes/Tests/Sandbox_PlayerMovement.unity`.
- Largest logical face: 64x64 cells (4,096 authoritative floor cells); smaller faces use adaptive grids.
- Largest visual projection: 256x256 RGBA32, uploaded at most once per frame.
- Estimated persistent memory per face: at most 768 KiB CPU and 256 KiB GPU texture storage.
- Sustained benchmark: 600 stamps average below 1 ms CPU each, at most 1 KiB managed allocation after warm-up,
  and texture upload submission below 3 ms in PlayMode automation.
- EditMode: 24 passed, 0 failed.
- PlayMode: 18 passed, 0 failed.
- Off-center visual/logical alignment is covered by an explicit planar projection test.
- Vertical wall impact resolution and authoritative visual stamping are covered by PlayMode automation.
- Windows development build succeeded and excludes sandbox scenes.
- Documentation: `docs/13_TERRITORY_PAINTING.md`.
- Developer interactive review approved on 2026-08-28 after floor/wall alignment, manga readability, FPS,
  spawn recovery, and state-colored HUD checks.

## Completion log

- 2026-08-21 - Implemented registered floor territory, world/grid mapping, CPU-authoritative stamps,
  Ice/Fire/Mist visual projection, reset, coverage and bank HUD, player sampling, element switching, projectile
  integration, bounded-memory reporting, and sustained-spray tests. Automated validation passed; awaiting
  developer playtest.
- 2026-08-27 - Developer review exposed that cube UVs displayed logical paint at unrelated floor locations
  and that walls needed authoritative paint rather than decorative circles alone. Replaced cube texture
  projection with explicit planar face surfaces for floors, walls, ramps, platforms, beams, steps, and tunnel
  geometry. Validation passed 24 EditMode, 16 PlayMode, and the Windows build.
- 2026-08-28 - Developer review found that opaque neutral face overlays erased structure readability. Neutral
  pixels now discard to reveal lit gray geometry, every structure uses shared manga-style base and bold
  inverted-hull outline materials, and the HUD shows smoothed FPS above element state. Validation passed
  24 EditMode, 17 PlayMode, and the Windows build.
- 2026-08-28 - Developer approved the manga outline/readability direction and requested `#FCFCFA` structure
  bases plus fall recovery. Updated the shared base material, added a labeled outlined spawn pad, and added
  deterministic player respawn below the arena. Validation passed 24 EditMode, 18 PlayMode, and the Windows
  build; awaiting final spawn/base-color review.
- 2026-08-28 - Spawn review found the world-space label oversized and back-facing, while white HUD text lost
  contrast against `#FCFCFA`. Flipped and reduced the spawn label, changed the territory/FPS HUD to dark
  green with a black outline, and revalidated 24 EditMode, 18 PlayMode, and the Windows build.
- 2026-08-28 - Colored Ice and Fire percentage labels by element and made the complete `Standing on` line
  follow Neutral, Ice, Fire, or Mist. The developer reported that the result looked really good and authorized
  the Territory Painting commit. Final validation passed 24 EditMode, 18 PlayMode, and the Windows build.
